# Removes Omnis method comments from text, so a class/lib name mentioned only in a comment
# is not mistaken for a target. Handles full-line comments (# …) and inline comments (## …).
# @? a '##' inside a string literal ('… ## …') is treated as a comment too — ignored as unlikely
# pText → the method text. Returns the text with comment portions removed (line structure kept).

Calculate lines as split(pText,kCr,kTrue) ## one row per line
Calculate result as ''
For loop from 1 to lines.$linecount step 1
	Calculate oneLine as lines.[loop].C1
	
	# inline comment: drop everything from '##' to end of line
	If pos('##',oneLine)
		Calculate oneLine as mid(oneLine,1,pos('##',oneLine)-1)
	End If
	
	# full-line comment: a line that (after leading whitespace) starts with '#' → blank it
	If left(jst(oneLine,'-'),1)='#'
		Calculate oneLine as ''
	End If
	
	Calculate result as con(result,oneLine,kCr)
End For

Quit method result